
build firmware/gpl: take rt-n66u and rt-n56u as an example:

1. change directory to uppler level of git repository
   so far in git server, git repository is /media/ASUSWRT/asuswrt, 
   so, cd /media/ASUSWRT

2. ./asuswrt/buildtools/autobuild rt-n66u rt-n56u   

   # build firmware only  
   # then, it will do: 
   #   build rt-n66u and rt-n56u
   #   cp image file to //192.168.123.98/Projects/ASUSWRT 
   #   cp image file to local directory /media/ASUSWRT/Firmware
   #   cp image file to ~/Dropbox/Working/Firmware/ASUSWRT


   ./asuswrt/buildtools/autobuild tag rt-n66u rt-n56u  

   # builld firmware/gpl to sq, 
   # ** please make sure build no in version.conf is odd number **
   # ** so that, firmware will be released with even build no.  **
   # you can modify autobuild's $backupdir, $releasedir, if they are changed.

   # then, it will do:
   #   bulid rt-n66u and rt-n56u with increased build No. in version.conf
   #   generate gpl tar file
   #   cp image/gpl files to //192.168.123.98/Public/ASUSWRT
   #   cp image/gpl files to //172.21.130.61/Software/RT-N66U/Firmware

   ./asuswrt/buildtools/autobuild gpl rt-n66u rt-n56u
   # build gpl only

   
   ./asuswrt/buildtools/autoliveupdate [model_name][firmware_version]
   
   #example: autoliveupdate rt-n16_3.0.0.1_1 rt-n66u_3.0.0.1_1 (could input one model or both at once)	
   #compare firmware version in wlan_update.txt which copy from //172.21.130.61/Software/RT-N66U/Firmware_LiveUpdateTest/
   #if it has new firmware version, it will update firmware version in wlan_update.txt
   #zip image file and copy to //172.21.130.61/Software/RT-N66U/Firmware_LiveUpdateTest/


build firmware with special purpose, ex, a new software project

1. create branch with keyword swpj-[Project], ex, asuswrt-swpj-misc-tools
	git branch asuswrt-swpj-misc-tools
	git checkout asuswrt-swpj-misc-tools

2. create control file with the same name
	please refer to ./asuswrt/release/src/router/APP-IPK/AiCloud-ipk/CONTROL/control to create
	./asuswrt/release/src/router/APP-IPK/misc-tools/CONTROL/control

	* modify "Version:" in control to control the version

3. add tag in each version updated by using autobuild tools to release
	setup ASUSWRTRELEASEDIR environment variable to the path of SQ release directory, ex
		export ASUSWRTRELEASEDIR="/mnt/tp-fs-11/Software/RT-N66U/Firmware_SQ"
	seutp ASUSBACKUPDIR environement variable to the path of backup directory,ex 
		export ASUSWRTBACKUPDIR="/mnt/sharing/Projects/ASUSWRT
	change directory to uppler level of git respostory and build firmware, ex
		cd /media/ASUSWRT
		./asuswrt/buildtools/autobuild tag rt-n66u
